# Binary

<Aside title="Placeholder">

This page is a stub. A systemd unit example is still being written.

</Aside>

The server is a single compiled binary with no runtime interpreter. Deploying it is a matter of getting the binary onto the host, giving it the environment it needs, and supervising the process.

The shape of a binary deployment:

- Install the newest stable release with `wyrd server install`, download a release bundle yourself, or build with `cargo build --release -p wyrd-server`.
- Provide the environment from [Configuration](/self-hosting/configuration/), including external Postgres, storage, and a signing key.
- Run it under a supervisor (systemd, or your platform's equivalent) that sends `SIGTERM` on stop so the server drains gracefully. Set the stop timeout above `WYRD_SHUTDOWN_DRAIN_MS`.

A systemd unit example will land here.

## Release bundles

Each GitHub release publishes one bundle per supported host, holding `wyrd-server` and the built UI under `ui/build`:

| Host | Bundle |
| --- | --- |
| macOS, Apple silicon | `wyrd-server-aarch64-apple-darwin.tar.gz` |
| macOS, Intel | `wyrd-server-x86_64-apple-darwin.tar.gz` |
| Linux (glibc), x86_64 | `wyrd-server-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.gz` |
| Linux (glibc), aarch64 | `wyrd-server-aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.gz` |

`checksums.txt` lists each bundle's SHA-256, and `checksums.txt.sig` is a raw Ed25519 signature over it from the Wyrd release key. `wyrd server install` checks that signature with the key built into the CLI, checks the bundle's digest, and only then extracts it under `<wyrd config dir>/server/versions/<version>` and points `server/current` at it. A failed download, signature, digest, or extraction leaves the previous installation active. To verify a manual download the same way:

```sh
openssl pkeyutl -verify -pubin -inkey release-signing-key.pem -rawin \
  -in checksums.txt -sigfile checksums.txt.sig
shasum -a 256 --check --ignore-missing checksums.txt
```

`release-signing-key.pem` is `crates/wyrd/wyrd-cli/src/server/release-signing-key.pem` in the Wyrd repository.

